  "notes": [
    "We reserve export in expression positions while preserving property and module-name contexts.",
    "Intrinsic import type queries retain named call, member, arguments, object and pair shapes.",
    "The intrinsic import path requires a string literal. Optional attributes use the compiler's with/assert container; outer trailing commas and arbitrary option keys are refused.",
    "Intrinsic call/member types are primary types, supporting array and lookup suffixes without duplicating the upstream type-level import fallbacks.",
    "Ordinary call expressions are unchanged.",
    "Reserved export remains a property name, including generated service signatures.",
    "TypeScript compiler syntax rejects Annex B HTML comments; removing that extra preserves HTML-shaped JSX attribute strings.",
    "Intrinsic import types retain a terminal type-argument list on the module reference or qualified member; generic arguments cannot be followed by another member."
  ],
